---
export const prerender = true;

import Base from '../../layouts/Codeforge.astro';

const title = 'Build with WebMCP in the OpenAI WebMCP Challenge';
const description =
  'Build an agent-native web app, test it in ChatGPT, and submit it by September 3.';
---

<Base
  {title}
  {description}
  article={{
    publishedTime: '2026-08-25T11:00:00-07:00',
    authors: ['Alex Nahas'],
    tags: ['WebMCP', 'OpenAI', 'hackathon'],
  }}
>
  <article class="challenge-post">
    <header class="challenge-post__header">
      <a href="/blog/" class="challenge-post__back">MCP-B / Blog</a>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="challenge-post__dek">{description}</p>
      <div class="challenge-post__byline">
        <span>Alex Nahas</span>
        <time datetime="2026-08-25">August 25, 2026</time>
        <span>3 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="challenge-post__body">
      <p class="challenge-post__lead">
        The OpenAI WebMCP Challenge is open. From August 25 through September 3, builders can
        create a new agent-native web app or add WebMCP to an existing one, then use it with
        ChatGPT's in-app browser.
      </p>

      <p>
        WebMCP is an experimental open web proposal that lets a site publish structured tools for
        an agent. The site defines the actions, inputs, and descriptions. The person and the agent
        stay in the same live app, so the work remains visible and sensitive actions can still ask
        for confirmation.
      </p>

      <div class="challenge-post__callout">
        <p><strong>Submission window</strong></p>
        <p>
          Submissions close September 3 at 1 p.m. PT. Check the
          <a href="https://webmcp.devpost.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
            >official competition page</a
          > for current rules, eligibility, prizes, and deadlines.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>What to build</h2>

      <p>
        Start with one workflow your app already understands. A good WebMCP tool should let an
        agent complete a meaningful task with fewer steps while keeping the result easy for a
        person to inspect and change.
      </p>

      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Pick a real task.</strong> Search, compare, create, update, or submit something
          your app already owns.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Expose the smallest useful tool surface.</strong> Give each tool a clear name,
          description, and input schema instead of mirroring every button on the page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Test the human-agent handoff.</strong> Let the agent do the mechanical work, then
          keep review, edits, and sensitive confirmations visible in the product UI.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p>
        The judging rubric looks at WebMCP leverage, execution, potential impact, and creativity
        and ambition. A focused workflow that feels finished will beat a wide tool surface with no
        clear user benefit.
      </p>

      <h2>Use MCP-B or the browser API directly</h2>

      <p>
        You can build directly against the proposed <code>document.modelContext</code> API. MCP-B
        adds open-source packages for typed tool registration, React integrations, polyfills,
        transports, and browser tooling when your app needs them.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          New to the project? <a href="https://docs.mcp-b.ai/start-here/choose-your-path"
            >Choose a path through the docs</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          Adding tools to a live product? Follow
          <a href="https://docs.mcp-b.ai/how-to/add-tools-to-an-existing-app"
            >Add tools to an existing app</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          Unsure which package layer fits? <a href="https://docs.mcp-b.ai/how-to/choose-runtime"
            >Choose a runtime</a
          >.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Key dates</h2>

      <dl class="challenge-post__dates">
        <div>
          <dt>Kickoff livestream</dt>
          <dd><time datetime="2026-08-25T15:00:00-07:00">August 25 at 3 p.m. PT</time></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Community office hours</dt>
          <dd><time datetime="2026-08-31T11:00:00-07:00">August 31 at 11 a.m. PT</time></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Submissions close</dt>
          <dd><time datetime="2026-09-03T13:00:00-07:00">September 3 at 1 p.m. PT</time></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Winners announced</dt>
          <dd><time datetime="2026-09-23">September 23</time></dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <h2>Build something only WebMCP makes practical</h2>

      <p>
        Focus on what people can do when an agent understands the app's real actions and works
        through the same interface they use. Pick that moment, make it reliable, and submit it.
      </p>

      <div class="challenge-post__actions">
        <a
          class="challenge-post__primary-action"
          href="https://webmcp.devpost.com/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer">Enter the challenge <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
        >
        <a href="https://docs.mcp-b.ai">Open the MCP-B docs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .challenge-post {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .challenge-post__header {
    max-width: 64rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8rem) clamp(1.5rem, 6vw, 5rem) clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }

  .challenge-post__back {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .challenge-post__header h1 {
    max-width: 18ch;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.97;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .challenge-post__dek {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.4rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .challenge-post__byline {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .challenge-post__body {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem) clamp(1.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .challenge-post__body > * + * {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .challenge-post__body p,
  .challenge-post__body li,
  .challenge-post__body dd {
    color: var(--foreground);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .challenge-post__lead {
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.45rem) !important;
    line-height: 1.6 !important;
  }

  .challenge-post__body h2 {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.6rem);
    font-weight: 650;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .challenge-post__body ol,
  .challenge-post__body ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
  }

  .challenge-post__body a {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .challenge-post__body code {
    border-radius: 0.2rem;
    background: var(--muted);
    padding: 0.15em 0.35em;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  .challenge-post__callout {
    margin-block: 2.5rem;
    border-left: 0.25rem solid var(--primary);
    background: var(--muted);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .challenge-post__callout p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .challenge-post__callout p + p {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  .challenge-post__dates {
    display: grid;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .challenge-post__dates div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(11rem, 1fr) minmax(13rem, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .challenge-post__dates dt {
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .challenge-post__dates dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .challenge-post__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .challenge-post__actions .challenge-post__primary-action {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    border-radius: 0.15rem;
    background: var(--primary);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 0.7rem 1rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .challenge-post__dates div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
